// What lies on the ground when the valley is created (D15).
//
// material:     an id from materials.ron, quoted.
// terrain:      grass | forest | ford (water and rock hold nothing).
// per_thousand: pieces per thousand tiles of that terrain that satisfy
//               `near`, when given.
// near:         only within so many tiles (eight-way steps) of a terrain:
//               things lie where they come from.
//
// Hide, meat and bone come from animals; logs from felled trees: no rule.
// Nothing ready-made lies about (the project lead, 10 November 2026):
// berries will be picked from the bushes, fibres made from gathered
// plants, flint broken from the rock. Only what the ground itself drops
// stays: dead wood under the trees, pebbles by the water. Flint lies on
// the banks and by the rock (D57, the project lead, 24 November 2026:
// "C'est parfait"): picked up, it cuts. Placeholder densities, a fifth of
// the pebbles'.
[
    // Dead wood under the trees.
    (material: "branch", terrain: forest, per_thousand: 60),
    // Pebbles on the banks and in the ford.
    (material: "pebble", terrain: grass, per_thousand: 90, near: Some((terrain: water, within: 4))),
    (material: "pebble", terrain: ford, per_thousand: 200),
    // Flint on the banks, and at the foot of the rock.
    (material: "flint", terrain: grass, per_thousand: 20, near: Some((terrain: water, within: 4))),
    (material: "flint", terrain: grass, per_thousand: 20, near: Some((terrain: rock, within: 3))),
    (material: "flint", terrain: forest, per_thousand: 20, near: Some((terrain: rock, within: 3))),
]
